# dummy-petshop local secrets — copy to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler dev`.
#
# Neither of these is required to run locally: the generated wrangler.jsonc
# already pins a fixed PETSHOP_SEAL_KEY under `vars` (the shop holds only fake
# data, so a stable dev key beats per-run plumbing), and the backdoor is open
# when PETSHOP_BACKDOOR_SECRET is unset. Set them here only to mirror a
# deployed env locally. Deployed envs get real values from Doppler at deploy
# time (scripts/deploy.ts); see apps/os/docs/integrations-and-secrets-design.md §7 S0.

# Seals every OAuth code and token (AES-256-GCM, src/seal.ts). 32 random bytes,
# base64: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Rotating it only invalidates outstanding
# fake tokens, which specs re-mint anyway.
PETSHOP_SEAL_KEY="ZHVtbXktcGV0c2hvcC1sb2NhbC1kZXYtc2VhbC1rZXk="

# When set, every /__backdoor/* route requires this exact value in the
# `x-petshop-backdoor` request header (403 otherwise). Leave unset locally to
# keep the backdoor open.
# PETSHOP_BACKDOOR_SECRET="choose-a-shared-secret"
